# `power::OpfResult`

Optimal generation, voltages, flows, prices and diagnostics.

## Signature

```cpp
power::OpfResult
```

## What It Does

The result of `opf`. Arrays keep the leading scenario axes of the grid.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `generation_p` | The optimal active output of each generator, `[..., generator]`. |  |
| `generation_q` | The optimal reactive output, `[..., generator]`. |  |
| `voltage` | Complex bus voltages, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `magnitude` | Voltage magnitudes, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `angle` | Voltage angles in radians, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `injection` | Complex net injection at each bus, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `from_power` | Complex power entering each line at its sending end, `[..., line]`. |  |
| `to_power` | Complex power entering each line at its receiving end, `[..., line]`. |  |
| `objective` | The optimal cost, `[...]`. |  |
| `p_price` | The multiplier of the active power balance at each bus: the cost of one more per-unit of demand there, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `q_price` | The multiplier of the reactive power balance, `[..., bus]`. |  |
| `from_shadow` | The multiplier of the sending-end rating, `[..., line]`; nonzero only for a binding rating. |  |
| `to_shadow` | The multiplier of the receiving-end rating. |  |
| `converged` | True when the optimiser met both tolerances. |  |
| `iterations` | Iterations used. |  |
| `constraint_violation` | The largest violation of the constraints at the returned point. |  |
| `first_order_optimality` | The first-order optimality measure. |  |
| `message` | A description of why the optimiser stopped. |  |

## Returns

Returned by `opf`.

## Errors

Reading a field does not solve again.

## Interpretation and Use

The objective of an unconverged result is the cost of the least-violating point, not an optimum. At an optimum every unconstrained generator runs where its marginal cost equals the price of power at its bus.

